{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSdcv2WkMNDdv73qnpEq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my analysis of the codebase, I now have a complete picture:\n\n**Requirement, restated:** Add a `POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` endpoint that transitions active orders to cancelled status, cancels associated created shipments, rejects cancellation if any shipment is confirmed (with 409), handles idempotent retries, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity (Order.kt:11-16): No status field exists\n- OrderController (OrderController.kt:21-34): Has create, getById, list; needs cancel method\n- OrderRepository (OrderRepository.kt:10-27): In-memory ConcurrentHashMap store\n- Shipment entity (Shipment.kt:9-14): Already has status with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED states\n- ShipmentController (ShipmentController.kt:26-44): Has create, getById, list; needs order validation\n- ShipmentRepository (ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27): In-memory store; needs findByOrderId method\n- Error handling (ApiError.kt:31-37, ApiExceptions.kt:1-30): Uses ErrorCode enum and ConflictException/ResourceNotFoundException\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- All error responses use ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ConflictException for 409, ResourceNotFoundException for 404)\n- Tests use MockMvc and verify both status AND response body structure (error code)\n- In-memory repositories using ConcurrentHashMap\n- Test classes reset state before each test with @BeforeEach\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. Order.kt - Add status field (unavoidable, required for storing state)\n2. OrderRepository.kt - Add method to find shipments by orderId (unavoidable, needed by cancel logic)\n3. OrderController.kt - Add cancel endpoint (required by ticket)\n4. ShipmentRepository.kt - Add method to find shipments by orderId (required by cancel logic)\n5. ShipmentController.kt - Add order status check on create (required by ticket)\n6. ApiError.kt - Add error codes for cancel conflicts (required for error envelope consistency)\n7. OrderControllerTest.kt - Add cancel endpoint tests (required)\n8. ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Add shipment-on-cancelled-order test (required)\n\n**Risks:**\n- Order status field is new; must default to ACTIVE to match existing behavior\n- Must ensure order status persists and is returned by GET /orders/{orderId}\n- Concurrent cancel and shipment creation could race (mitigated by in-memory store semantics)\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket is clear on all required behaviors.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field (default ACTIVE), create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderIdWithShipments(orderId)` helper or make ShipmentRepository handle finding shipments by orderId\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments for an order\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method that:\n   - Finds the order (404 if not found)\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with the order (idempotent)\n   - Check all shipments for the order\n   - If any is CONFIRMED, throw ConflictException with 409\n   - Otherwise, set order to CANCELLED and cancel all CREATED shipments\n   - Return the cancelled order with 200\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Modify create method to:\n   - Check if the order exists (already does this implicitly by not validating)\n   - Check if the order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with 409\n   - Continue with normal shipment creation\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add new ErrorCode values:\n   - ORDER_CANCELLED (for when trying to create shipment on cancelled order)\n   - ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT (for when trying to cancel an order with confirmed shipments)\n\n**Alternative approaches considered and rejected:**\n\n- **Alternative: Store cancelled status in separate set** - Rejected because it adds complexity; a single status field is cleaner and follows the shipment pattern\n- **Alternative: Don't add status to Order model, only track in repository** - Rejected because the ticket explicitly requires GET /orders/{orderId} to report the status\n- **Alternative: Throw generic CONFLICT error code** - Rejected because the existing API uses specific error codes (ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS) for clarity; should follow that pattern\n- **Alternative: Ignore order validation in shipment create** - Rejected because ticket explicitly requires rejecting shipment creation for cancelled orders\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Cancel ACTIVE order with no CONFIRMED shipments:**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - OrderController.cancel() called\n   - Find order (ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - Check shipments for order\n   - If none are CONFIRMED, set order.status = CANCELLED\n   - For each CREATED shipment, set status = CANCELLED\n   - Save updated order and shipments\n   - Return 200 with updated Order (JSON includes status: CANCELLED)\n\n2. **Cancel already CANCELLED order:**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - OrderController.cancel() called\n   - Find order\n   - If already CANCELLED, return 200 with order unchanged\n   - No database changes\n\n3. **Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment:**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - OrderController.cancel() called\n   - Find order\n   - Check shipments, find CONFIRMED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT)\n   - Return 409 with error envelope\n   - No changes to order or shipments\n\n4. **Create shipment for CANCELLED order:**\n   - POST /shipments\n   - ShipmentController.create() called\n   - Check if order is CANCELLED\n   - Throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANCELLED)\n   - Return 409 with error envelope\n   - No shipment created\n\n5. **Cancel non-existent order:**\n   - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel\n   - OrderController.cancel() called\n   - Find order\n   - Order not found\n   - Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - Return 404 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest additions:**\n   - Test cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 and changes status to CANCELLED\n   - Test cancelled order's shipments are set to CANCELLED\n   - Test cancelling already CANCELLED order returns 200 and changes nothing\n   - Test cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Test cancelling non-existent order returns 404\n   - Test GET /orders/{orderId} after cancel includes status field\n\n2. **ShipmentControllerTest additions:**\n   - Test creating shipment for CANCELLED order returns 409 with error envelope\n   - Test error code is ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the design. Let me start with the Order entity:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2281,"cache_read_input_tokens":23641,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2281},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83b4d0d6-98a2-4d8b-833c-b182dc09618e","uuid":"59131674-d6bf-40eb-9a37-857285f409d8","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:50:49.626Z","request_id":"req_011CfSdcudTAUF3hYshn2DGF"}
