rId}/cancel\")` method with full cancel logic including idempotent retry and all-or-nothing semantics. Required by ticket.\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Added `findByOrderId(orderId)` method to query shipments by order. Required to check shipment statuses during cancel.\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: Added OrderRepository dependency and order status check in create method to reject CANCELLED orders. Required by ticket.\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added ErrorCode.ORDER_CANCELLED and ErrorCode.ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT. Required for error envelope consistency.\n- **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Added 6 new tests covering all cancel scenarios. Required for acceptance criteria 3 and 5.\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Added 1 new test covering shipment creation on cancelled order. Required for acceptance criteria 5.\n\n**No unresolved findings** - all functionality implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders, cancels their CREATED shipments, rejects cancellation if any shipment is CONFIRMED, handles idempotent retries, and prevents shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt: Added status field with ACTIVE/CANCELLED enum\n              OrderController.kt: Added cancel endpoint with idempotent and all-or-nothing semantics\n              ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method to query by order\n              ShipmentController.kt: Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 6 tests for cancel functionality\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 1 test for shipment-on-cancelled-order rejection\n\nTests         1. \"cancels an active order and returns 200\" - POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel returns 200 with CANCELLED status\n              2. \"cancelled order is persisted and retrievable\" - GET /orders/{orderId} after cancel returns CANCELLED status\n              3. \"cancelling an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing\" - Idempotent retry succeeds\n              4. \"cancelling non-existent order returns 404\" - Unknown order returns ORDER_NOT_FOUND error\n              5. \"cancelling order with created shipments cancels those shipments\" - CREATED shipments are transitioned to CANCELLED\n              6. \"cancelling order with confirmed shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\" - All-or-nothing: 409 prevents any changes\n              7. \"rejects shipment creation for cancelled order with 409\" - POST /shipments for CANCELLED order returns ORDER_CANCELLED error\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, Tests run: 20, Failures: 0, Errors: 0\n              All existing tests continue to pass; 7 new tests added and pass\n\nNot done      Nothing - all acceptance criteria implemented and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":238,"cache_read_input_tokens":52980,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":238},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"83b4d0d6-98a2-4d8b-833c-b182dc09618e","uuid":"bcbe55f9-8d58-46de-9efe-86d5796c4ab3","timestamp":"2026-09-26T19:53:13.503Z","request_id":"req_011CfSdohv4wv6SWjpQwQEkD"}
